<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hērōus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡρῳος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to a hero</i>, <i>heroic.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 7, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chelys,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 3, 102</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					1, 8, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3, 3</span></i> (4, 2), 16: versus, <i>heroic</i> or <i>epic verse</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Leg. 2, 27, 68</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 5, 28</span></i>: pes, <i>an heroic</i> or <i>epic foot</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 47,
			182</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			As <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hērōus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>an epic
			verse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apte Jungitur herous cum breviore modo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 17, 22</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 20, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in herois,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 88</span></i>
			 Zumpt <i>N. cr.;</i> also: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">herous, qui est idem dactylus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 9, 4, 89</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hērōum</span></b> ,
				i, n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A monument to the memory of a hero</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 10, 5,
				6, § 18</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> = asphodelus, <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				22, 32, § 67</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
